{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>I have sunk in miry deep</b> — יון is mire, like מטיט היון, and there is no standing. The ayin has a ḥatef kamatz, as though it had a full kamatz gadol, and it ought to have had a pataḥ, since it is a noun. R. Moses said: it is a noun on the pattern of מוקטר מוגש, and it changed because of the guttural letter." "<b>And the flood</b> — like: the river." "<b>And the meaning of it swept over me</b> — I was almost swept away, and it will sweep me away, in the manner of ונשמה לא נותרה בי. And the proof that afterward he prays אל תשטפני."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 69, :notes {0 "The phrase כמו היה מעמד במרכבה is textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:33:22.404992610Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}